{:id "0060-lab-markers-recede"
 :title "Lab dress: the asterisks of a dressed stress recede"
 :lupa/deps #{"0052-lab-dress" "0058-lab-flick-ui"}
 :lupa/area :lab
 :lupa/risk :low
 :goal "Ben's first screenshot of the lab on WebGPU (2026-11-18) reads
        '*this* is great!' with 'this' in gold and its two asterisks at
        full strength either side. Once the stress is dressed the
        asterisks have done their work. Flair may not drop a character
        (the charter), but it may quieten one: the two asterisks rest
        whispered, arriving and leaving with the dress they belong to."
 :scope ["src/halfahead/lab/dress.cljc" "test/halfahead/lab/dress_test.cljc"
         "src/halfahead/lab/pose.cljc" "test/halfahead/lab/pose_test.cljc"
         "e2e/lab.mjs" "docs/LAB.md"]
 :design "lab.dress/placed: a :gilt, :rubric or :strong dress whose span
            is enclosed by asterisks (the unit just before the span and
            the unit just after it are both '*', each a glyph of its own)
            gains :markers [id-before id-after] on its placed entry.
            Every other entry is as now, and so is the order, so
            window.__lab.dress() and the overlay's dress line read as
            they do today.
          lab.pose, where a placed dress becomes letters at rest: the
            marker glyphs of a placed dress wear the look of :whisper
            (lab.dress/looks), with the same weight over time as the
            dress they belong to. Where nothing is dressed (level 0, or
            a style too spare to dress the stress) they are ordinary
            letters. A marker that lies inside another placed dress
            keeps that dress.
          Tests: placed for '*this* is great!' (gilt on 'this', :markers
          the two asterisks' ids); for '**bold**' (the inner pair); a
          stress in capitals has no :markers; a whispered aside has
          none. pose: with the dress placed and at full weight both
          asterisks are at whisper's size and ink and the letters
          between them are gold; with no dress they are as any letter;
          every existing pose and dress test passes unchanged.
          e2e/lab.mjs, in the dress step, after 'This is *the one thing*
          that matters (trust me).' has come to rest in Plain on paper:
          the two asterisks' glyphs in lastFrame() are in the muted ink
          and smaller than the letters beside them, and the text box
          still holds both asterisks.
          docs/LAB.md: one sentence under Dress."
 :acceptance
 ["dress and pose tests as in the design, on both hosts; `bb test` stays
   green"
  "`bb lab:e2e` passes with the added check and every existing step"]
 :non-goals
 ["No character is hidden, dropped or changed; the textarea's text is
   untouched"
  "No change to what marks/dress-for returns, to marks, score, the
   schema, the renderer or lab.main"
  "Do not run `bb e2e` or `bb play`"]
 :context ["src/halfahead/lab/dress.cljc" "test/halfahead/lab/dress_test.cljc"
           "src/halfahead/lab/pose.cljc" "e2e/lab.mjs" "docs/LAB.md"
           "DESIGN.md"]
 :budget-usd 8.0}
